                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "NOT RECOMMENDED - it tries to be a narrative-driven horror game while having an extremely weak and unfounded story. It is pretty much: \"there is this girl and paranormal things happen.\"\n\nThe overall theme with the issues of the game is that it is not fun. The pay-off simply is not there.\n\nThe game completely falls apart in the gameplay. The item management is horrendously laborous in that you can only hold one item in your hand and you have to drop that item before you can open a door or defend yourself from instakill borderline invisible Cthulhu ghosts. That turns the game into an annoying management sim where you have to pedantically plan and execute everything to not lose progress.\n\nThen there is Chapter 4 where the enemy is a teleporting Slender Man that will kill you just by you turning your back to it and every time it does you have to painstakingly re-obtain your camera.\n\nThere are a way too many annoying things to mention in detail such as every single scenario being repetitive re-run of three levels of practically identical level layouts. It is a loop game - prepare for massive samey boredom. With tons of bugs. For example, dropping anything in stairs can permanently lose it. The game is not well optimized. It runs poorly even if you lower the resolution by a lot.\n\nUPDATE: I played through the game and it gets even worse at the end. The fifth chapter adds a frame rate reducing crawler enemy that is impossible to hit if the game lags even a little. There are plenty of other annoyances and questionable game designs that reduce fun potential. The endings make no difference and change nothing from the status quo. \"Suffering\" will be the main descriptor of what playing this game feels like. AVOID AVOID AVOID.\n\nOh and it runs poorly frame-rate-wise for an Unreal Engine 4 game with a low object and character count. It becomes so bad at times that it becomes impossible to hit anything that is moving even a little.",
